course: dictionary
lesson: 9562
title: Straight: one word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have several meanings, and the context tells you which one the writer means. The first meaning of straight is not bent or curved. «The Rat walks ahead on the straight grey road» tells you the road has no bends.
explain: Straight can also mean at once, without stopping: «go straight home». The word home is the clue, because it tells you where to go and the word straight tells you how directly. In «a straight answer», straight means honest, so the answer is clear and true.
explain: Check your meaning by putting it into the sentence. In «three days straight», straight means in a row with no break. Ask yourself: did it happen three days in a row? If yes, your meaning fits.
fact: Straight means not bent or curved, and it can also mean at once or honest.
fact: «Straight hair» has no curls.
fact: «A straight line» is the shortest way between two points.
fact: In maths, a straight angle is 180 degrees, and polygons have straight sides.
fact: Reflective strips shine headlights straight back to the driver, so a child in dark clothes can be seen from far away.
exercise: «In cricket the bowler keeps the arm straight.» What does straight mean here? | Curly | Very fast | *Not bent | Honest
exercise: «She gave me a straight answer.» What does straight suggest? | Curly | *Honest and clear | Long and thin | Quick and noisy
exercise: «Ravi went straight home after school.» What does straight mean here? | *At once, without stopping | Bent round the corner | Ravi's hair has no curls | In a row with no break
test: «The road ran straight across the flat fields.» What does straight mean here? | Wet with rain | Covered in mud | Very dark | *Going in one direction, not bent
test: «It rained for three days straight.» What does straight mean here? | Very quickly | Honest and clear | *In a row with no break | Sideways
exam: «A straight line is the shortest way between two points.» What is a straight line? | A curly line | A slow way round | *The shortest way between two points | A bent path with many turns
